According to \cref{prop:qpe-from-cdf}, $
abla_{ m{x}}F_{Y\mid m{X}}+ m{\psi}_{Y\mid m{X}}\,p_{Y\mid m{X}}=0$. Under assumptions of smoothness and strict positivity, taking the partial derivative w.r.t. $y$ gives  egin{align} 
abla_{ m{x}}p_{Y\mid m{X}}+\partial_y ig( m{\psi}_{Y\mid m{X}}\,p_{Y\mid m{X}} ig)&= rac{
abla_{ m{x}}p_{Y\mid m{X}}}{p_{Y\mid m{X}}}+ rac{p_{Y\mid m{X}}\,\partial_y m{\psi}_{Y\mid m{X}}+ m{\psi}_{Y\mid m{X}}\,\partial_yp_{Y\mid m{X}}}{p_{Y\mid m{X}}}
onumber\&=
abla_{ m{x}}\log p_{Y\mid m{X}}+ m{\psi}_{Y\mid m{X}}\,\partial_y\log p_{Y\mid m{X}}+\partial_y m{\psi}_{Y\mid m{X}}=0, \end{align} which means the equation holds when $ m{\xi}= m{\psi}_{Y\mid m{X}}$. Additionally, according to \cref{prop:qpe-from-cdf} again, $ m{\psi}_{Y\mid m{X}}\,p_{Y\mid m{X}}=
abla_{ m{x}}F_{Y\mid m{X}}$, so  egin{align} \lim_{y	o+\infty} m{\psi}_{Y\mid m{X}}\,p_{Y\mid m{X}}=\lim_{y	o+\infty}
abla_{ m{x}}F_{Y\mid m{X}}=
abla_{ m{x}}\lim_{y	o+\infty}F_{Y\mid m{X}}=\lim_{y	o+\infty}1=0. \end{align} The case for $y	o-\infty$ is analogous. From \cref{eq:qpepde-1} and \cref{eq:qpepde-2}, the necessity of the lemma is established. Now, for any $ m{\xi}$ satisfying the conditions, subtract the equation it satisfies from the equation that $ m{\psi}_{Y\mid m{X}}$ satisfies to obtain \[( m{\xi}- m{\psi}_{Y\mid m{X}})\,\partial_y\log p_{Y\mid m{X}}+\partial_y( m{\xi}- m{\psi}_{Y\mid m{X}})=0.\] Then, multiply both sides of the equation by $p_{Y\mid m{X}}$ and expand $\partial_y\log p_{Y\mid m{X}}$, which yields \[( m{\xi}- m{\psi}_{Y\mid m{X}})\,\partial_yp_{Y\mid m{X}}+p_{Y\mid m{X}}\,\partial_y( m{\xi}- m{\psi}_{Y\mid m{X}})=\partial_y ig(( m{\xi}- m{\psi}_{Y\mid m{X}})\,p_{Y\mid m{X}} ig)=0.\] Integrating this w.r.t. $y$ from some $y_0$ gives \[( m{\xi}- m{\psi}_{Y\mid m{X}})\,p_{Y\mid m{X}}+C=0,\] where $C( m{x})$ is a function independent of $y$. Taking $y	o+\infty$ for this equation on both sides, since $\lim_{y	o+\infty} m{\xi}\,p_{Y\mid m{X}}=0$ and $\lim_{y	o+\infty} m{\psi}_{Y\mid m{X}}\,p_{Y\mid m{X}}=0$, it follows that $\lim_{y	o+\infty}C=C=0$. Thus, $( m{\xi}- m{\psi}_{Y\mid m{X}})\,p_{Y\mid m{X}}=0$ holds for all $ m{x},y$. Due to the strict positivity assumption, $p_{Y\mid m{X}}>0$, so it must be that $ m{\xi}- m{\psi}_{Y\mid m{X}}=0$, which establishes the sufficiency of the lemma.

